WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.020
Observable sovereign AI is about visibility with restraint.

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:12.520
Teams need enough information to operate responsibly, investigate failures, tune performance, review access decisions, and improve workflows.

3
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:23.260
At the same time, telemetry should not become the next privacy problem or an uncontrolled copy of sensitive prompts, outputs, retrieved content, and tool activity.

4
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.220
Start by mapping the workflow.

5
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:35.400
Identify user requests, model paths, retrieval paths, tool paths, queues, workers, hardware, storage, and outputs.

6
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.340
Decide what signals answer real operating questions.

7
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:50.720
Logs, metrics, traces, audit records, alerts, dashboards, and review notes each have a role, and none of them should be used as a reason to collect everything.

8
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.080
Safe telemetry requires design.

9
00:00:53.180 --> 00:01:02.940
Use structured events, redaction, conservative defaults, controlled debug logging, access limits, retention rules, and privacy-aware tracing.

10
00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:12.880
Track model versions, workflow context, resource health, permission decisions, and incident signals without exposing more content than the investigation requires.

11
00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:15.880
Finally, turn telemetry into action.

12
00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:25.340
Review dashboards, tune alerts, create backlog items, assign owners, govern evidence handling, and update monitoring as workflows change.

13
00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:33.600
Sovereign AI succeeds when teams can operate with confidence, preserve data control, and explain what happened when review is needed.
